Nothing went wrong and nothing needs you. Two of the control model's scoring jobs were bumped by higher-priority jobs and have rejoined the queue on their own. I launched nothing.

**What happened**
- At 07:20 the cluster cancelled two of the control's seed-43 scoring jobs to free their GPUs for other work. The control is the model trained on 256-token chunks. The two jobs:
  - The documents scoring had answered 1,030 of 1,500 questions.
  - The photos scoring had answered all 1,500 and its judge (the Qwen3-8B model that grades answers) was at 816.
- Both went back into the queue automatically. They will start again from scratch, because the scoring script cannot resume.
- The photos job left an ungraded answer file on disk. It is not a result, and the restarted job will overwrite it.
- The code the scores depend on is unchanged.

**Where things stand**
- **The model trained on 1,024-token chunks:** its first training stage is healthy. It has seen 580,800 of 1M documents and should finish around 09:00 tomorrow (2026-11-14). Its next loss check is around 18:55 today.
- **The control's 6 final scoring jobs** (3 test sets × 2 seeds, 1,500 questions each): all are waiting in the queue. The scheduler expects them to start between 15:15 and 17:00 today.
- **Budget:** about 10.8 of 38 GPU-days used. The full plan projects to about 35.

**What I recorded**
- A note in the experiment log for each cancelled job, a progress point for the long-chunk training, and an updated row in the campaign's known-issues list.
- A request to this project's other chats: when a scoring job is cut off after answering every question, it should only re-run the judge, not answer everything again. This saves GPU time on every cut-off; it blocks nothing.
- A complaint about the monitoring tool: it woke this loop for a job the cluster had already put back in the queue, while every check said OK. This happened twice today.
- I also fixed a claim the automatic checker flagged in the status file. The 3.3-point gap between the two seeds on 300 questions is one observation, not a measure of noise. At that size no gap is a result; only the paired test on 1,500 questions decides.

**Next wake:** when all 6 scoring jobs have left the queue, or in 18 hours at most. Then I record the 6 scores and fill in the control's row of the results table.

Nothing needed from you.
